      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page (from [[write-journal]]) describes a mechanism that provides transaction-like safety for file writes in the Grimoire system. Specifically, it explains:\n\n- **How it works**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records the file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or a marker indicating it did not exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal.\n\n- **Rollback capability**: If an agent run fails (due to turn cap, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every write in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed before, and deleting any newly created files.\n\n- **All-or-nothing semantics**: This gives each run atomic write semantics without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself acts as the transaction log, existing only in the process\u0027s memory for one run\u0027s duration.\n\n- **Query agent exception**: The Query agent never uses the journal\u0027s rollback functionality since it has no write tool at all; the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library but is only populated by agents that actually write.",
      "input_tokens": 5354,
      "output_tokens": 249
    }
